ld black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]enumeration[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_kind_filter[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_kind_filter: add a defaulted `kind` field to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`ArtifactRefRepositoryWire` and skip `kind == \"sidecar\"` repositories in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`append_commit_candidates` before spawning `git log`, leaving [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`resolve_commit` and every other kind untouched.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The host labels each repository and proves both surfaces agree[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]host_repo_kind[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_kind_filter[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]host_repo_kind: carry `RepoRecord.kind` into `ArtifactRefRepository` and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its wire form in `artifact_ref_context()`, extend the prompt-bar/LSP [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parity test with a sidecar repository, assert sidecar resolution still [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]succeeds, and correct the two documentation sentences that promise [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commits from every local checkout.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Raise the published sase-core-rs floor[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_floor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after host_repo_kind[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_floor: once the release carrying `core_kind_filter` is published, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]raise the `sase-core-rs` lower bound in `pyproject.toml` so an installed[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase cannot silently run the unfiltered enumeration.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ek","hidden":false,"llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","phase_bead_id":"sase-ek.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-c